<title>UK: Wet Brent trades firmer at March - 2 cents.</title>
<headline>Wet Brent trades firmer at March - 2 cents.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-02-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>A wet Brent cargo traded at March Brent -2 cents on Wednesday, sharply higher than recent traded levels, dealers said.</p>
<p>The cargo, loading March 6-8, was one of the Brents nominated from the paper chains on Wednesday. It was kept by a European major ahead of the five o'clock deadline and sold on to a Wall Street trader which already holds two or three cargoes.</p>
<p>--Rosalind Russell, London Newsroom +44 171 542 5387</p>
